{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), giving us essentially no information about whether the image modality contributes predictive signal or whether multimodal fusion is beneficial. The central question for this multimodal cellular profiling study is whether combining image with RNA improves over RNA alone. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal, clean extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), the same profile setting (singleprofile), and adds only the image modality with a standard ResNet50 and simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of adding the image modality. If config_016 substantially outperforms 0.485, it justifies investing further in multimodal configurations and image encoder/aggregation choices; if it does not, it redirects the search toward RNA-only improvements (better encoders, multiprofile aggregation). This is the highest-information-gain experiment given the near-total absence of evidence about the image modality's contribution."
}

